sec.p:
To this end, this study analyses survey data from 350 non-technical BI users in Vietnam. Trust in the AI capabilities of BI software is negatively associated with self-reported verification behaviour (
β = − 0.196
), whereas verification behaviour is positively associated with perceived decision quality (
β = 0.220
). Within the specified model, the resulting negative indirect association partially offsets the positive direct association between trust and perceived decision quality, so that the total association is approximately 14% smaller than the direct association. The direct association between perceived system explainability and verification is not statistically significant, and the hypothesized moderating role of AI literacy received no statistical support.
